## Reading and writing files.
##
## Reading a file that is not there, or writing where the host does not
## allow it, is undefined. Call `exists` first.
#
# The filesystem, as the host provides it. Every type here is an Int, a
# String or a Bool, so the boundary carries all of it on every target
# (docs/modules.md, "What may cross the boundary") -- which is why this
# library needs no Pyking half at all.
#
# Reading a file that is not there, or writing where the host will not
# let you, is *undefined*: Pyking has no exceptions and no option type,
# so there is nothing this module could answer with. Ask `exists`
# first. See docs/libraries.md.

## Reads the whole file at `path` as text. Reading a file that does not
## exist is undefined, so check with `exists` first.
##
## # Parameters
## - `path`: the file, relative to the directory the program runs in, or
##   absolute.
##
## # Returns
## The file's contents.
##
## # Examples
## ```pyking norun
## import fs
## fs.write_text("notes.txt", "milk\neggs\n")
## if fs.exists("notes.txt"):
##     print(fs.read_text("notes.txt"))
## ```
## ```stdout
## milk
## eggs
##
## ```
public def read_text(path: String) -> String

## Writes `text` to the file at `path`, replacing what it held, and
## creating it if it does not exist. Writing where the host does not
## allow it is undefined.
##
## # Parameters
## - `path`: the file, relative to the directory the program runs in, or
##   absolute.
## - `text`: the new contents.
##
## # Examples
## ```pyking norun
## import fs
## fs.write_text("greeting.txt", "hello")
## print(fs.read_text("greeting.txt"))
## ```
## ```stdout
## hello
## ```
public def write_text(path: String, text: String) -> ()

## Tells whether there is a file at `path`.
##
## # Parameters
## - `path`: the file, relative to the directory the program runs in, or
##   absolute.
##
## # Returns
## `true` when the file exists, `false` otherwise.
##
## # Examples
## ```pyking norun
## import fs
## print(fs.exists("no-such-file.txt"))
## ```
## ```stdout
## false
## ```
public def exists(path: String) -> Bool
